            <ArticleTitle>[Avulsion fracture of the serratus anterior muscle in a golfer].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>56-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">V05130277</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Golf is a sport with much repetitive actions often causing overuse injuries. We report a case of a left side avulsion fracture of the anterior serratus at the insertion on costa 4-6. A professionel golfer experienced sudden onset of pain of the chest during a golfswing. Clinically the patient had winging of the scapula and pain at the lateral side of costa 4-6. Ultrasonography showed an avulsion fracture of costa 5 at the insertion of the anterior serratus. The patient was referred to scapula-stabilising rehabilitation and fully recovered.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
